  "answer": "The following documents provide evidence for typical Growth and Enterprise onboarding timelines:\n\n- **NL-005-S02** explicitly defines the typical timelines: **Growth Plan Onboarding is 4–6 weeks** and **Enterprise Plan Onboarding is 8–10 weeks**, including a phase-by-phase target week table [NL-005#NL-005-S02].\n- **NL-012-S06** reports observed median onboarding durations: **Mid-Market/Growth plan: 5.2 weeks** and **Enterprise plan: 8.7 weeks**, with segment-level averages and sample customer durations [NL-012#NL-012-S06].\n- **NL-031-S03** validates those segment averages from a tracked sample: Mid-Market average **5.2 weeks** and Enterprise average **8.7 weeks** [NL-031#NL-031-S03].\n- **NL-011-S06** documents Q2 averages: **Mid-Market segment averaged 5.2 weeks** and **Enterprise averaged 8.7 weeks**, with permission mapping as a major enterprise friction point [NL-011#NL-011-S06].\n- **NL-015-S04** confirms the **Enterprise average of 8.7 weeks** and notes that sales continues to promise a **4-to-6 week rollout**, which is consistent with the typical Growth Plan timeline [NL-015#NL-015-S04].\n\nTogether, these documents show both the planned typical timelines (Growth 4–6 weeks; Enterprise 8–10 weeks) and the observed averages (Growth 5.2 weeks; Enterprise 8.7 weeks).\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
